# CQ 06: Which artefact is a model, and which training produced it?
#
# The label of a model instance is the relative path of the file it stands for,
# models/ProductionNet_v1.onnx in the worked example. That is how the
# dissertation ties the abstract model to what is actually deployed: a name in
# the graph is a path in the project.
#
# The question therefore asks for the name rather than for a place. A model has
# no relation to a resource, and adding one would state something the model
# does not know: where a file lies is a matter for the deployment, not for the
# description of the system.
PREFIX iso22989: <https://w3id.org/aias/odp/iso22989#>
PREFIX rdfs:     <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
SELECT ?model ?artefact ?training ?algorithm
WHERE {
  ?model a ?mk . ?mk rdfs:subClassOf* iso22989:Model .
  OPTIONAL { ?model rdfs:label ?artefact . FILTER(lang(?artefact) = "en") }
  OPTIONAL { ?model iso22989:isCreatedBy ?training .
             OPTIONAL { ?training iso22989:basedOnAlgorithm ?algorithm } }
} ORDER BY ?model
